<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ivangorod</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1492">1492</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ivangorod is a town in Leningrad Oblast, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narva">Narva</a> River opposite the Estonian city of Narva. Its fortress was founded in 1492 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iii">Ivan III</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, after whom it is named, facing the Livonian castle across the river. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> held it in 1581–1590 and 1612–1704, and it became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a> between 1919 and 1945.</p></div>
